<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GDALMM:0</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Information</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Provides information about the file in a format importable via GDAL/OGR.</ows:Abstract>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:File import with GDAL/OGR libraries"/>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:Imports vector or raster files in any format compatible with GDAL/OGR into the MiraMon format. The user has the option to choose whether to import only specific layers or all layers contained in the file. An output directory can be specified, or, if the file contains a single layer of a single type, an output filename can be provided with the corresponding extension: pnt, arc, pol, or img."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Provides information about a file via GDAL/OGR..</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>DirOFitEntrada</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>GDAL/OGR file or folder to import</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File o directorio to import using GDAL/OGR libraries.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:InputFoldOrFile"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:GDALMM:1</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Importing a file using GDAL/OGR libraries.</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Import the file/folder, or a subset of its elements, using GDAL/OGR libraries.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Imports a file into MiraMon via GDAL/OGR.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>DirOFitEntrada</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>GDAL/OGR file or folder to import</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>File o directorio to import using GDAL/OGR libraries.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:InputFoldOrFile"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxLListaCapes</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Layer list file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Text file containing a list of layers, bands, raster subdatasets and/or tables to import. If this file is not specified, all information found in the source file will be imported.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:LayerListFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-lst</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-lst</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/plain</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TIPUS_SORTIDA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Output type</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Allows determining whether the output is a directory (D) or a file (F). By default, it will always be a directory. Use the F option only when you want to import a single vector layer or a raster dataset, and the result of this import is a single layer in MiraMon format.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>F</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>D</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>D</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>AJUSTA_AMPLADA_CAMPS</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Fit field widths</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Allows adjusting the width of both numeric and text fields to the minimum required. For numeric fields, the new number of decimals is chosen to preserve the highest value that ensures the presence of non-zero digits.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#boolean">boolean</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
					<DefaultValue>FALSE</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>BANDA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Band</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>In the case of a raster file, it refers to the reference (0 indexed) band to which the selection is to be applied. If the band is not indicated, the first reference band will be used. If multiband output is selected, all bands from the same data subset that have the same grid spacing as the reference band will be written.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>DirectoriSortida</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Output folder</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Output directory or file (as specified via /TIPUS_SORTIDA=) where the files imported to MiraMon format will be written.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:OutputFoldOrFile"/>
				<LiteralOutput>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#anyURI">anyURI</ows:DataType>
				</LiteralOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
</wps:ProcessDescriptions>